{"duration_api_ms":242380,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"edbef7bc-e466-4a68-91f7-18e6646fae32","total_cost_usd":0.288682,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15447,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":22689,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":17302},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":15447,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":22689,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15447,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":15447},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":22689,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":15447,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.288682,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":17302,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"observation\":\"The feasible front is one ridge: D≈3.38 m, bluntness 1.2, cone 70° (all at the upper limit), with only flight-path angle varying from -1.5 to -3.56. Three constraints bind at once. Peak g caps |gamma| near 3.57, the mass-fraction margin at D=3.38 is only 0.003, and bluntness/cone cannot go beyond (1.2, 70) without geometry or hull failures. Round-3 hypervolume gain was only 0.0043, so the remaining upside is (a) squeezing D and gamma to their exact limits and (b) checking whether slightly lower bluntness or cone at the corner changes T.\",\"evidence\":[\"C-6ffb6b7edb43 (D 3.384) has mass margin 0.000736 and C-d20e6439cf38 (D 3.38) has 0.003097. That is about 0.59 per m, so the zero crossing is near D≈3.3852; D=3.385 should still be feasible.\",\"C-e6bfb3db2b24 (-3.56, g 11.981) and C-480359711777 (D 3.36, -3.57, g 11.989) give dg/d|gamma|≈1.75 per deg and dg/dD≈0.5 per m. That puts the g=12 limit near gamma≈-3.569 at D=3.385.\",\"T falls about 9.7 K/deg with steeper gamma (C-41b2ddb7397c to C-e6bfb3db2b24) and about 18 K/m with larger D (C-465478728e6f vs C-e6bfb3db2b24). hf falls about 119 kW/m² per m of D.\",\"Geometry failures: C-05edbf22eaa2 (b 1.25), C-3d41ce848a30 (b 1.21) and C-7db223121090 (cone 69) fail the aero-surrogate hull. C-e0197c1bd7dc (cone 68) has an overlapping nose sphere and shoulder torus. So (1.2, 70) sits at a vertex of the valid region.\",\"Mass fraction scales about D² with a shape factor near 1 at (1.2, 70). It is roughly 1.02 at C-36f9165b9496 (b 0.87, cone 65) and 1.11 at C-ab9827dc6929 (b 0.4, cone 53), so the corner is the best place for large D.\"],\"mechanism\":\"Bondline T is set by heat-pulse severity: it falls with lower ballistic coefficient (larger D, higher-Cd blunt 70° cone) and with steeper entry. g and mass fraction cap gamma and D, and the corner (1.2, 70) maximises Cd and minimises shield mass. The gains left are therefore small: D→3.385 and gamma→-3.567 lower T by about 0.15 K and hf by about 0.4k. Points at the same D along the gamma ridge then replace the current front points. Stagnation heat flux should go roughly as Rn^-0.5, which I am taking from prior knowledge rather than from the data. Lowering bluntness at cone 70 should therefore raise hf, but the effect on T is unmeasured. I probe it at fixed gamma=-3.5 so the effect can be isolated.\",\"uncertainty\":\"g at gamma≈-3.567 is within about 0.0005 of the limit, so tiny model errors could flip feasibility. The mass-fraction zero crossing is extrapolated linearly by 0.001 m. The hull shape below (1.2, 70) is unknown, so some bluntness/cone probes may return no geometry. The b^-0.5 heating scaling and the shape-factor model for mass fraction are assumptions, not fitted.\",\"proposals\":[{\"parent_id\":\"C-e6bfb3db2b24\",\"rationale\":\"Push D to the mass limit (3.385) and gamma to just inside the g limit; the best expected corner point.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.385,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.567},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":274500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.11,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests the exact mass and g limits; the best possible improvement to the front end.\",\"requested_fidelity\":1},{\"parent_id\":\"C-e6bfb3db2b24\",\"rationale\":\"Slightly safer gamma at D=3.385 to hedge the g limit.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.385,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.564},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":274420,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.14,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Hedge in case -3.567 crosses g=12 or the mass limit.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-e6bfb3db2b24\",\"rationale\":\"D=3.3845 gives slightly more mass margin (about 0.0004) with gamma near the g limit.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3845,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.568},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":274580,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.11,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Alternate hedge combining D and gamma near both limits.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-e6bfb3db2b24\",\"rationale\":\"Same larger D at a lower |gamma| to lower hf while keeping T near the current front.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.385,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.55},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":274090,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.28,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Shifts the front knee toward lower hf.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-d20e6439cf38\",\"rationale\":\"D=3.385 refresh of the mid-high gamma part of the front.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.385,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.45},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":271700,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.25,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Uniform D improvement should dominate the existing neighbours.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-7ae520b30cfb\",\"rationale\":\"D=3.385 refresh at gamma -3.3.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.385,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.3},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":268060,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393.77,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Extends the improved front toward lower hf.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-a00857fd77d0\",\"rationale\":\"D=3.385 refresh at gamma -3.0.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.385,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":260850,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":397.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Front coverage in the middle of the trade-off.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-b48a9ba7e9b0\",\"rationale\":\"D=3.385 refresh at gamma -2.5.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.385,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":248935,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":403.05,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Front coverage in the mid-low hf region.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-f552e60ec816\",\"rationale\":\"D=3.385 refresh at gamma -2.0.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.385,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":237500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":410.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Front coverage toward the low-hf end.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-d67ebd910866\",\"rationale\":\"Low-|gamma| end of the front with larger D; should improve on the lowest-hf point slightly.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.385,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":227100,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":417.9,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"The extreme end of the front sets the hf extent of the hypervolume.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-e6bfb3db2b24\",\"rationale\":\"Small bluntness reduction at the corner (b=1.19) with D reduced to keep mass margin; tests whether the hull allows b<1.2 at cone 70 and the sensitivity of hf and T to b.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.37,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.19,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":275800,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.1,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Cheap check of local sensitivity to bluntness at cone 70.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ab6fb1629c20\",\"rationale\":\"b=1.16 at cone 70, D 3.35, gamma -3.5. Isolates the bluntness effect against the b=1.2 baseline.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"bluntness_ratio\":1.16,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":281800,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.7,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Measures dT/db and dhf/db near the corner.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ab6fb1629c20\",\"rationale\":\"b=1.12 with the same D and gamma to extend the bluntness sweep.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"bluntness_ratio\":1.12,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":286800,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Second point of the bluntness sweep.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ab6fb1629c20\",\"rationale\":\"b=1.08 with the same D and gamma to extend the bluntness sweep.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"bluntness_ratio\":1.08,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":292000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393.3,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Third point of the bluntness sweep.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ab6fb1629c20\",\"rationale\":\"b=1.0 at cone 70 with smaller D (3.3) to absorb the higher mass-fraction shape factor.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":310000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":394.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Checks whether lower bluntness costs T or hf strongly and whether the hull allows it.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ab6fb1629c20\",\"rationale\":\"b=0.9 at cone 70 with D 3.3; probes the far end of the bluntness range with the surrogate.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.9,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":327000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":395.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Provides a wide-baseline bluntness sensitivity point.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ab6fb1629c20\",\"rationale\":\"Slightly lower cone (69) at b=1.15 to map the hull boundary and the effect of cone on T.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"bluntness_ratio\":1.15,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":69.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":283000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests whether lower bluntness opens cone values below 70, and the Cd effect on T.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ab6fb1629c20\",\"rationale\":\"b=1.1 with cone 67, D 3.3. Should be valid geometry since the minimum cone falls with bluntness (about 65 at b=1.1).\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.1,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":67.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":295000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":395.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Maps the hull and the sensitivity of T to cone angle.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ab6fb1629c20\",\"rationale\":\"b=1.0 with cone 65, D 3.3; a second cone-sensitivity point at lower bluntness.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.0,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":65.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":315000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":396.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Assesses whether lower cone angle ever helps T; likely confirms the corner optimum.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ab6fb1629c20\",\"rationale\":\"b=0.9 with cone 64, D 3.3, near the known-valid region around C-36f9165b9496 (b 0.87, cone 65).\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.9,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":64.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":330000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":397.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Anchors the cone/bluntness sensitivity in a region likely inside the hull.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0}]}","ttft_ms":199566,"type":"result","duration_ms":242443,"uuid":"db79ffd6-da58-4f0c-8fa5-eb841fe8b354","ttft_stream_ms":1776,"time_to_request_ms":57,"first_content_frame_ms":1776,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
